<aside class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-red-500/35 bg-red-500/8 p-5 text-sm leading-6 text-skin-base/80" aria-label="Safety and limitations">
  <h3 class="font-bold text-skin-base">Safety and limitations</h3>
  <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
    <li>This tool provides planning estimates only. It is not a substitute for a qualified electrical design, inspection or local code compliance.</li>
    <li>Use the exact manufacturer datasheet for the panel, MPPT, battery, inverter, fuse, cable and charger you intend to install. Do not select hardware from the result alone.</li>
    <li>Verify cable ampacity after insulation temperature, conduit, bundling, ambient temperature, installation method and length derating. The larger voltage-drop result is not automatically safe.</li>
    <li>Every fuse and breaker must be DC-rated for the system voltage and interrupt current, correctly sized to protect the cable, and installed according to the equipment manufacturer’s maximum fuse rating.</li>
    <li>Check battery BMS continuous and peak charge/discharge limits, low-temperature charging restrictions, ventilation, terminal torque and the complete fault-current path before energizing the system.</li>
    <li>For PV systems, verify cold-weather Voc, Isc, MPPT start voltage, maximum PV voltage/current, shading and string configuration. For AC shore power or inverter output, use a qualified electrician and the applicable local standards.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mt-4 border-t border-red-500/20 pt-3 text-xs text-skin-base/65">If any input is unknown, stop and obtain the datasheet or professional verification before purchasing or wiring components.</p>
</aside>
